 \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*),leftmargin=2em]
-  \item The queries to $f$ for primes $p > c$ number at most $c\,K_c\,(L+t)(L+1)^{E_W(c)}$ (on every branch, with $L$ replaced by $\lfloor\ell/\log_2(c+1)\rfloor$; Appendix~\ref{app:tb-counts}). Sylow subgroups with $e_p = 1$ use one run of the recursion of Section~\ref{sec:recursion} on the chart (a \emph{core call}), of dimension $n_p$, with the arities of Remark~\ref{rem:combined-schedule} in place of the Schedule~1 arities of Theorem~\ref{thm:main} and with the error split of Section~\ref{sec:recursion}, whose solver third is now used at the Schedule~2 grades. Those with $e_p > 1$ use the recursion of Theorem~\ref{thm:ring-to-field}(iii) on the chart, with that run on each socle section and at most $n_p$ calls. The primes $p \le c$ add the queries of~\cite[Theorem~1]{ImranIvanyos2023}, $\poly(\log|G|)$. No other step queries $f$.
+  \item The queries to $f$ for primes $p > c$ number at most $c\,K_c\,(L+t)(L+1)^{E_W(c)}$ (on every branch, with $L$ replaced by $\lfloor\ell/\log_2(c+1)\rfloor$; Appendix~\ref{app:tb-counts}). Sylow subgroups with $e_p = 1$ use one run of the recursion of Section~\ref{sec:recursion} on the chart (a \emph{core call}), of dimension $n_p$, with the arities of Remark~\ref{rem:combined-schedule} in place of the Schedule~1 arities of Theorem~\ref{thm:main} and with the error split of Section~\ref{sec:recursion}, whose solver third is now used at the Schedule~2 grades. Those with $e_p > 1$ use the socle recursion of Corollary~\ref{cor:black-box-pe} (Proposition~\ref{prop:tb-recursion}, the recursion of Theorem~\ref{thm:ring-to-field}(iii)) on the chart, with that run on each socle section and at most $n_p$ calls. The primes $p \le c$ add the queries of~\cite[Theorem~1]{ImranIvanyos2023}, $\poly(\log|G|)$. No other step queries $f$.
